# Blank — UI structure

Minimal app shell with the **full `internal/ui` registry tree** for staging reusable UI.
On-disk index: **`internal/ui/README.md`** (same `registry:*` labels as FastyGoUI).

```
internal/ui/
  layout/       # registry:layout — document/chrome shells + request data
                #   root_layout.templ, topnav_layout.templ, dashboard_layout.templ
                #   shell_head.templ, header_trailing.templ
                #   data.go (Data, Document(), Topnav(), Dashboard()), build*.go
  components/   # registry:components — icon/, toggles/, navigation/, appsidebar/
  blocks/       # registry:blocks — marketing/hero/, … (full scaffolds)
  widgets/      # registry:widgets — UI + behavior (staging stub)
  variants/     # registry:variants — wireframe utility maps (staging stub)
  utils/        # registry:utils — app helpers on templ/utils
internal/views/
  <page>.templ  # route page — views.<Page>(d layout.Data, f fixtures.Locale)
internal/site/
  router.go     # PageSpec route manifest (Body: views.<Page>)
  render.go     # handlePage, web.Render
  nav.go        # nav from route specs
  layout_data.go # thin wrapper → layout.BuildData
  feature.go    # Feature wiring only
internal/fixtures/
  locale/*.json # i18n copy
```

| Path | Role |
|------|------|
| `internal/ui/layout` | Document frame + named chrome layers, request `Data`, head/trailing partials |
| `internal/ui/components` | Props-only UI; no HTTP or fetch |
| `internal/ui/components/appsidebar` | Local sidebar used inside `DashboardLayout` |
| `internal/ui/blocks/<domain>/` | Full scaffolds (e.g. `marketing/hero`); **not** empty adapters |
| `internal/ui/widgets` | Behavior shells → future `fastygo/widgets` (stub) |
| `internal/views/<page>.templ` | Page composition — `views.<Page>(d, f)` |
| `internal/site` | Runtime routing; not a registry |

**Page composes layout.** Open `views/<route>.templ` and you see the full two-layer tree.

**Named layout layers in `internal/ui/layout/`:**
- `layout.RootLayout` — document frame only (`html`, `head`, `body`).
- `layout.TopnavLayout` — header, main, footer, mobile sheet.
- `layout.DashboardLayout` — TopnavLayout + desktop aside slot.

Add new layout layers in `internal/ui/layout/` only when a route needs structurally different app chrome. Section scaffolds belong in `internal/ui/blocks/<domain>/<organism>/`.

**Forbidden:**
- `internal/ui/recipes`, `internal/ui/elements`, `internal/ui/ui/`, `internal/ui/blocks/layout/`.
- 4-line `blocks/*` packages that only call `@layout.TopnavLayout { @body }`.
- Central `views/models.go` or `views/layout_helpers.go` — co-locate per page instead.
- `views.*From` wrapper functions — pages are `views.<Page>(d, f)` directly.

**views** receive resolved strings/structs only — no `fixtures.LoadLocale` inside `.templ`.

When adding a page:

1. Extend `fixtures.Locale` and every `locale/*.json`.
2. Add `internal/views/<page>.templ` — `templ <Page>(d layout.Data, f fixtures.Locale)` composing `@layout.RootLayout` + `@layout.TopnavLayout` or `@layout.DashboardLayout`.
3. Add one `PageSpec` in `internal/site/router.go` with `Body: views.<Page>`.
